{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He shall bring the pledge out to you.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: it is not the way of a borrower to bring out anything but the least of his utensils, and from here we derive that a creditor collects from the lowest grade property (z'vurit); but the Sages of blessed memory enacted that he may collect from middle-grade property (b'nonit), so that the door not be locked before borrowers. And if he did not wish to bring out the pledge, he is coerced to fulfill the positive commandment, just as one is coerced regarding all the other commandments; and likewise the court descends to sell his lands and pay the lender."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:49.396780452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}